    "message": {
      "content": "# Validation Checklist for Multi-Node Language-Model Serving Systems\n\n## Purpose and Scope\n\nThis checklist validates that a distributed LLM serving system (tensor-parallel, pipeline-parallel, expert-parallel, or data-parallel deployments) behaves correctly under load, fails predictably, and reports honestly. It is written for pre-production acceptance and post-change regression testing. Each item is phrased as a verifiable assertion with a concrete evidence artifact.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Configuration Identity\n\n**Goal: Prove that every node believes it is running the same system.**\n\n- [ ] **1.1 Model artifact hash match.** Record SHA-256 of model weights, tokenizer files, and config files on every node. All hashes must be identical. Evidence: hash manifest per node, diffed programmatically (not by eyeball).\n- [ ] **1.2 Code and build identity.** Record git commit, build ID, container image digest (not tag \u2014 tags are mutable), and CUDA/NCCL/driver versions per node. All must match. Note: driver versions may legitimately differ across heterogeneous clusters; if so, verify the *supported* matrix explicitly rather than assuming.\n- [ ] **1.3 Parallelism topology agreement.** Every node must report the same values for tensor-parallel size, pipeline-parallel size, expert-parallel size, and data-parallel size, and its own rank within each dimension. Cross-check that the product of parallelism degrees equals the number of participating processes.\n- [ ] **1.4 Serving-parameter parity.** Sampling defaults, max context length, max batch size, KV-cache budget, quantization settings, and rope/scaling parameters must be identical across nodes. A single node with a different `max_num_seqs` or cache budget will produce load-dependent divergence that looks like a bug elsewhere.\n- [ ] **1.5 Configuration provenance.** The running configuration must be traceable to a versioned source (config",
      "reasoning": "",
